          guideText: `{name}. Today we turn to the most profound and tender question a human being ever faces: what does it mean to live well, knowing you will die? Every philosophical tradition has a serious answer. Stoicism, Epicureanism, Buddhism, existentialism, religious traditions — they disagree, but they've thought harder about this than almost anyone in ordinary life. This lesson doesn't pretend to resolve it. It asks you to sit with it honestly.`,
          headline: `Death and the Meaning of Life`,
